{"id": "AS-01", "dimension": "broad_synthesis", "question": "What does 21 CFR 820.10 require?", "answer_raw": "21 CFR 820.10 requires manufacturers to document a quality management system that complies with ISO 13485 and other applicable requirements, as well as comply with other applicable regulatory requirements. The requirements include (a) documenting a quality management system that complies with ISO 13485 and other applicable requirements, (b) complying with other applicable regulatory requirements in this title, including ISO 13485 Clause 7.5.8, 7.5.9.1, and 8.2.3, and (c) handling advisory notices in accordance with part 806. Additionally, manufacturers of class II, class III, and class I devices must comply with Design and Development requirements in ISO 13485, as appropriate. For devices that support or sustain life, compliance is required as appropriate, and enforcement applies to devices that meet the specified criteria.", "answer_final": "21 CFR 820.10 requires manufacturers to document a quality management system that complies with ISO 13485 and other applicable requirements, as well as comply with other applicable regulatory requirements. The requirements include (a) documenting a quality management system that complies with ISO 13485 and other applicable requirements, (b) complying with other applicable regulatory requirements in this title, including ISO 13485 Clause 7.5.8, 7.5.9.1, and 8.2.3, and (c) handling advisory notices in accordance with part 806. Additionally, manufacturers of class II, class III, and class I devices must comply with Design and Development requirements in ISO 13485, as appropriate. For devices that support or sustain life, compliance is required as appropriate, and enforcement applies to devices that meet the specified criteria.", "answer_shape": {"mode": "synthesis", "scope": "section", "exhaustive": false, "requested_units": ["21 CFR 820.10"], "focus_terms": [], "signals": [], "rationale": "an overview of 21 CFR 820.10"},